# GitHub issue / PR workflow

For every discrete change in this repo:

1. Open an **English** GitHub issue first. Implement on a branch. Open a PR. Link with `Closes #N`.
2. Do not commit straight to `master` / `main` except for the initial bootstrap.
3. Do not merge your own PR unless the user explicitly asks. Leave it for review.
4. Commit as the repo owner's existing git identity only. Never set an AI / Cursor / Copilot / ChatGPT author or committer. Never run `git config`.
5. Commit messages and PR / issue text: short, concrete, no AI filler, no mention of Cursor / Copilot / ChatGPT.
6. PR body: what changed, how you checked it, a short manual checklist.
7. Interactive tools (Streamlit, web apps) go in `apps/`. Algorithm code stays in `python/` and `c/`. The showcase frontend lives in `web/`.
